{"author":{"id":"6033ad3a62469493b79b19fe4fb66aa96b5a224ed38b3533d8d3f1b8cf68be03"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794013986,"nonce":"HHwTYtYDqFHtpJj+Nx47FlyJ7AE=","target":"8b52492121e24e05ce12093c269be0ab03014b8636d0548a8785bc920626c957","message":"## Goal\n\nRebuild the business-design registers and the relationship matrices of the KOT from the analysts' approved TO BE documents (231 processes, 2025 stories in «Реестр US»), and keep every other part of the approved May KOT (kot_2026-05-27) as it is.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Our work derives from the analysts' work, which the stakeholders already have, and the May KOT is approved. Change only what is strictly necessary.\n- Stories and actors are taken verbatim from the documents; no LLM writes or rewords them.\n- The technical section is frozen: components (7), component/technology (8), functions (13), information objects 10.1 and 10.2, and matrix (11). It changes only if a new story needs a component or an information object that does not exist; such a gap is triaged by hand before anything is changed.\n- New processes are expected not to introduce new bounded contexts. The pipeline must prove that by reporting stories that no existing component covers and information needs that no existing object covers.\n\n## Division of labour\n\n- Claude (meta assistant) prepares data, edits rake tasks, scripts and prompts, and keeps these issues. Claude checks its edits without LLM calls and without writing to work/ or out/: syntax checks, `rake -P` and `rake -n` for the wiring, and deterministic code run on scratchpad copies.\n- The user runs every rake task, LLM or not, in the order that debugging needs, and commits.\n- Each issue ends with «Your run»: the tasks that exercise the change and what to check. After a run, Claude reads the outputs (.err, .warn, check reports) and proposes the next edit.\n\n## Regenerated KOT items\n\n(2) roles, (3) participant/role, (4) user stories, (5) processes, (6) process/story, (9) component/participant, (12) story/component. Table (1) participants gains P-03.2.\n\n## Decisions (2026-11-07)\n\n1. IDs follow the analysts: story_id is {pid}-US-NN with NN taken from the analysts' «№» (КБП57 already writes KBP57-US-01). The analysts have no role IDs, so roles keep the May format {pid}-R-NN. Use-case IDs stay as written and are not in the KOT.\n2. Compound actors are split as in May (ТБП27, ТБП19, ТБП56): atomic singular roles, one participant each; a parenthesis clarifies the head noun (ТБП7 «Заявитель (ЛУВД, …)» became «Заявитель»). A story shows its actor verbatim in «Я как» and links to all of its roles.\n3. Role descriptions are written by the LLM, with the role prompt adapted to the new workflow.\n4. Use cases stay out of the KOT but are given to the LLM as context for component linking.\n5. Projections and aggregates stay frozen; only gaps are reported.\n6. Descriptions for KBP82–92 are short summaries of «Суть процесса», written by Claude as data preparation.\n7. Matrix (9) is derived per story: the story's roles' participants × its components.\n8. The three ТБП137 stories come from a hand-kept supplement file; their components are linked like all others.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nStage 6 regeneration, stage 7 (component/process), the narrative chapters, the KOT skeleton.\n\nChildren carry the label epic/nov-kot.","files":null}]}